//
// Ramsey formula ( the negation of it )
//
//  Find a graph G of size n such that there
//  is no clique of size k and no independent set of size m
//
//  E(i,j) is true if there is an edge between vertex i and j
//  A clique of size 3 is then expressed like 
//  E(1,2) & E(1,3) & E(2,3)
//

// There is no clique of size k
[ A i=subsets(k, 1..n) ] ![A j=subsets(2,i)] E(j)

AND

// F are edges in the complement graph G'

[ A j=subsets(2,1..n) ] ( E(j) XOR F(j) )

AND

// There is no clique of size m in the complement graph G'
[ A i=subsets(m, 1..n) ] ![A j=subsets(2,i)] F(j)
